Inject the nix store volume, its mount and NIX_CONFIG into the runner
container, following the pattern this chart already uses for DOCKER_HOST and
the GitHub TLS certificate: scan what the user supplied, and append only what
is absent. That is what keeps the wiring in place when a consumer overrides
template.spec.containers or template.spec.volumes, which Helm replaces
wholesale rather than merging.

A claim-backed store additionally needs an fsGroup, so securityContext comes
out of the passthrough loop to have one added.

kubernetes-novolume mode takes NIX_CONFIG without a volume, since asking for
no volumes is the whole point of it.

